1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,480
Clarifying issues is a behavior best used to summarize where the other person stands

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:11,100
in a way that helps him or her to make a decision to take action. You will not use this behavior

3
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:15,140
until you have enough information to reflect the other person's dilemma, to comment on

4
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:20,060
what's moving the person toward taking action and what's holding him or her back. This must

5
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:25,300
be done in a neutral and non-judgmental way, allowing silence to follow, so that the other

6
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:30,300
person can think about next steps. Your role, when you use this behavior, is to reflect

7
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:34,420
in a fair way what's going on with the other and then to trust him or her to take the action

8
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:39,340
that makes the most sense. Here are a few examples.

9
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:44,380
To summarize, you're really interested in helping with the project, and at the same

10
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:49,720
time you have a very heavy schedule and you don't see how you can fit it in.

11
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:54,180
Your dilemma is that you're open to changing the way we work together, but you're not sure

12
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:58,140
that the others on your team will be as willing.

13
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:03,980
On the one hand, you're supportive of my candidacy for the position, but on the other hand, you

14
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:07,500
don't want to take any active role on influencing the choice.

